@startuml
title Bonecutters S3 And CloudFront Hosting
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Owner" as Owner
component "Provisioning access\nhuman-approved" as Provisioning
component "Deployment access\nleast privilege" as DeployAccess
component "client/dist" as Dist
cloud "Private S3 bucket\nS3 REST origin" as S3
component "CloudFront OAC" as OAC
cloud "CloudFront distribution" as CloudFront
component "ACM certificate\nus-east-1" as Cert
cloud "www.bonecutters.us\ncanonical" as Www
cloud "bonecutters.us\nredirect to www" as Root
component "Config validator\nno AWS calls" as Validator

Owner --> Provisioning : creates resources
Owner --> DeployAccess : assumes for deploy
Dist --> DeployAccess : upload source
DeployAccess --> S3 : write static assets
DeployAccess --> CloudFront : create invalidation
CloudFront --> OAC : signs origin requests
OAC --> S3 : private read access
Cert --> CloudFront : viewer TLS
Www --> CloudFront : public site
Root --> CloudFront : redirect behavior
Validator ..> DeployAccess : checks local names only

note right of S3
Block Public Access remains enabled where feasible.
Do not use the S3 website endpoint for OAC.
end note

note bottom of DeployAccess
Deployment access is separate from provisioning access
and must not include SimpleETL resource permissions.
end note

@enduml
